WEBVTT

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:06.026
-Yes, Harry!
-Knew you wouldn't die. Lose a leg.

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:08.112
-Or an arm.
-Pack it in altogether?

00:00:08.195 --> 00:00:10.114
BOTH:
Never!

00:00:12.116 --> 00:00:13.450
SEAMUS:
Shush!

00:00:14.076 --> 00:00:16.578
Go on, Harry. What's the clue?

00:00:17.579 --> 00:00:20.457
-Who wants me to open it?
ALL: Yes!

00:00:21.208 --> 00:00:23.836
-Do you want me to open it?
-Yes!

00:00:35.097 --> 00:00:37.349
What the bloody hell was that?

00:00:41.478 --> 00:00:44.189
All right, everyone!
Go back to your knitting.

00:00:44.356 --> 00:00:48.485
This is gonna be uncomfortable enough
without all you nosy sods listening in.

00:00:51.613 --> 00:00:55.576
I reckon you have to be barking mad to
put your own name in the Goblet of Fire.

00:00:56.118 --> 00:00:58.746
Caught on, have you?
Took you long enough.

00:00:59.872 --> 00:01:01.999
I wasn't the only one
who thought you'd done it.

00:01:02.166 --> 00:01:04.334
Everyone was saying it
behind your back.

00:01:06.587 --> 00:01:09.882
Brilliant.
That makes me feel loads better.

00:01:10.758 --> 00:01:14.136
-Least I warned you about the dragons.
-Hagrid warned me about the dragons.

00:01:14.219 --> 00:01:15.846
No, no, no, I did.

00:01:16.013 --> 00:01:19.099
No, don't you remember?
I told Hermione to tell you...

00:01:19.183 --> 00:01:23.187
...that Seamus told me that Parvati
told Dean that Hagrid was looking for you.

00:01:23.353 --> 00:01:27.274
Seamus never actually told me anything,
so it was really me all along.

00:01:28.275 --> 00:01:31.278
I thought we'd be all right, you know...

00:01:31.528 --> 00:01:33.530
...after you'd figured that out.

00:01:34.031 --> 00:01:36.617
Who--? Who could possibly
figure that out?

00:01:37.201 --> 00:01:38.660
That's completely mental.

00:01:38.911 --> 00:01:41.997
Yeah. Isn't it?

00:01:42.164 --> 00:01:44.208
I suppose I was a bit distraught.

00:01:46.668 --> 00:01:48.378
Boys.

00:02:12.945 --> 00:02:14.238
BOTH:
Hi, Harry.

00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:20.577
Cho, Harry's looking at you.

00:02:24.456 --> 00:02:26.250
CHO:
Shush.

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:28.252
HERMIONE:
Look at this!

00:02:30.254 --> 00:02:32.714
I can't believe it! She's done it again.

00:02:33.841 --> 00:02:36.093
"Miss Granger,
a plain but ambitious girl...

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:39.054
...seems to be developing a taste
for famous wizards.

00:02:39.221 --> 00:02:41.348
Her latest prey, sources report...

00:02:41.598 --> 00:02:45.269
...is none other than the
Bulgarian bonbon, Viktor Krum.

00:02:45.477 --> 00:02:49.356
No word yet on how Harry Potter's
taking this latest emotional blow."

00:02:50.858 --> 00:02:52.192
Parcel for you, Mr. Weasley.

00:02:52.276 --> 00:02:54.361
Oh, thank you, Nigel.

00:02:59.283 --> 00:03:02.119
Not now, Nigel. Later.

00:03:03.954 --> 00:03:05.372
Go on.

00:03:10.752 --> 00:03:13.505
I told him I'd get him Harry's autograph.

00:03:15.757 --> 00:03:17.467
Oh, look, Mum's sent me something.

00:03:25.642 --> 00:03:27.394
Mum sent me a dress.

00:03:27.644 --> 00:03:31.398
Well, it does match your eyes.
Is there a bonnet? Aha.

00:03:31.982 --> 00:03:33.775
Nose down, Harry.

00:03:34.318 --> 00:03:38.280
-Ginny, these must be for you.
-I'm not wearing that, it's ghastly.

00:03:40.032 --> 00:03:41.783
What are you on about?

00:03:42.034 --> 00:03:43.994
They're not for Ginny.

00:03:44.161 --> 00:03:45.370
They're for you.

00:03:46.413 --> 00:03:50.334
-Dress robes.
-Dress robes? For what?

00:03:51.418 --> 00:03:55.005
McGONAGALL:
The Yule Ball has been a tradition...

00:03:56.548 --> 00:03:59.301
...of the Triwizard Tournament...

00:03:59.927 --> 00:04:02.012
...since its inception.

00:04:02.554 --> 00:04:06.433
On Christmas Eve night,
we and our guests...

00:04:06.683 --> 00:04:08.352
...gather in the Great Hall...

00:04:08.435 --> 00:04:12.522
...for a night of well-mannered frivolity.

00:04:14.191 --> 00:04:16.360
As representatives of the host school...

00:04:16.443 --> 00:04:21.531
...I expect each and every one of you
to put your best foot forward.

00:04:21.949 --> 00:04:24.534
And I mean this literally, because...

00:04:24.701 --> 00:04:29.331
...the Yule Ball is, first and foremost...

00:04:30.082 --> 00:04:31.458
...a dance.

00:04:35.796 --> 00:04:37.547
Silence!

00:04:37.798 --> 00:04:40.801
The house of Godric Gryffindor
has commanded the respect...

00:04:40.968 --> 00:04:43.553
...of the wizard world
for nearly 10 centuries.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:47.849
I will not have you, in the course of a
single evening, besmirching that name...

00:04:48.058 --> 00:04:52.354
...by behaving like a babbling,
bumbling band of baboons.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.856
Try saying that five times fast, huh?

00:04:55.107 --> 00:04:56.483
McGONAGALL:
Now, to dance...

00:04:56.733 --> 00:05:00.404
...is to let the body breathe.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:03.991
Inside every girl,
a secret swan slumbers...

00:05:04.199 --> 00:05:06.410
...longing to burst forth
and take flight.

00:05:06.618 --> 00:05:10.622
Something's about to burst out of Eloise
Midgen, but I don't think it's a swan.

00:05:10.831 --> 00:05:14.001
Inside every boy,
a lordly lion prepared to prance.

00:05:14.209 --> 00:05:16.378
-Mr. Weasley.
-Yes?

00:05:16.461 --> 00:05:19.006
Will you join me, please?

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:27.139
Now, place your right hand
on my waist.

00:05:27.389 --> 00:05:29.266
-Where?
-My waist.

00:05:30.475 --> 00:05:32.477
And extend your arm.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:35.022
Mr. Filch, if you please.

00:05:38.442 --> 00:05:40.110
One, two, three.

00:05:40.277 --> 00:05:43.655
One, two, three. One, two, three.

00:05:45.657 --> 00:05:47.242
HARRY:
Oi!

00:05:47.451 --> 00:05:49.494
Never gonna let him forget this,
are you?

00:05:49.661 --> 00:05:50.912
BOTH:
Never.

00:05:51.121 --> 00:05:52.456
McGONAGALL:
Everybody come together.

00:05:52.622 --> 00:05:54.916
Boys, on your feet!

00:06:18.065 --> 00:06:19.941
Why do they have to travel in packs?

00:06:20.192 --> 00:06:22.694
How are you supposed to get one
on their own to ask them?

00:06:30.577 --> 00:06:34.206
Blimey, Harry. You've slayed dragons.
If you can't get a date, who can?

00:06:34.456 --> 00:06:36.500
I think I'd take the dragon right now.

00:06:42.714 --> 00:06:44.424
I take after my mum.

00:06:44.508 --> 00:06:48.470
Though I didn't know her very well.
She left when I was about 3.

00:06:48.553 --> 00:06:50.514
No, not the maternal sort, her.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:54.351
Broke me dad's heart, though.
He was a tiny little fella, my dad.

00:06:54.518 --> 00:06:58.980
I could pick him up at the age of 6 with
one hand and put him up on the dresser.

00:06:59.231 --> 00:07:01.525
He laughed so hard at that.

00:07:03.527 --> 00:07:05.529
Very funny.

00:07:11.493 --> 00:07:15.122
And then he died
just when I started school, so....

00:07:15.372 --> 00:07:18.375
So I sort of had to make
me own way, as it were.

00:07:18.708 --> 00:07:20.877
But enough of me. What about you?

00:07:38.228 --> 00:07:43.358
This is mad. At this rate, we'll be
the only ones in our year without dates.

00:07:45.569 --> 00:07:48.363
Well, us and Neville.

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:51.158
Yeah, but, then again,
he can take himself.

00:07:51.783 --> 00:07:54.578
It might interest you to know
that Neville's already got someone.

00:07:57.581 --> 00:07:59.541
Now I'm really depressed.

00:08:05.297 --> 00:08:08.592
[WHISPERS] "Get a move on or all
the good ones will have gone."

00:08:10.677 --> 00:08:12.679
Who you going with, then?

00:08:15.557 --> 00:08:17.184
FRED: Oi, Angelina?
[MOUTHS] What?

00:08:17.434 --> 00:08:22.606
[WHISPERS]
Do you wanna go to the ball with me?

00:08:22.939 --> 00:08:24.649
To the ball?

00:08:24.816 --> 00:08:26.401
Yeah, all right.

00:08:30.071 --> 00:08:31.615
Oi, Hermione.

00:08:31.698 --> 00:08:33.533
You're a girl.

00:08:33.617 --> 00:08:34.910
Very well spotted.

00:08:35.076 --> 00:08:37.037
Come with one of us?

00:08:41.625 --> 00:08:44.586
Come on. It's one thing for a bloke
to show up alone.

00:08:44.669 --> 00:08:46.296
For a girl, it's just sad.

00:08:46.463 --> 00:08:50.217
I won't be going alone, because,
believe it or not, someone's asked me!

00:08:57.098 --> 00:08:59.100
And I said yes!

00:09:00.977 --> 00:09:02.562
Bloody hell.

00:09:02.646 --> 00:09:04.481
She's lying, right?

00:09:04.648 --> 00:09:05.690
If you say so.

00:09:06.608 --> 00:09:09.736
RON: Look, we've just gotta
grit our teeth and do it.

00:09:09.986 --> 00:09:12.072
Tonight, when we get back
to the common room...

00:09:12.239 --> 00:09:13.865
...we'll both have partners. Agreed?

00:09:14.115 --> 00:09:15.617
Agreed.
